[V phone, boot 11, dd on /dev/rufsroot0, read only] 16 KiB reads: 1 reader 40 MB/s, 4 readers 44 MB/s in all. 4 KiB: 13 MB/s, 17 MB/s in all. One slot, one mutex over command and copy.
Details in bsd/dev/laurel_ufs_queue.h. Writes stay in slot 0 behind the fence of 2950. Host test: scripts/laurel/test-ufs-queue.sh.
Line: LAUREL UFS QUEUE: on|off, one line a minute with the counts. Kill switch ufsqueue=0. The line also gives the link gear: 144 MB/s at 1 MiB looks like one HS-G1 lane [I].

